WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.400
Hello? Yes, this is he.

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:07.200
Him? Me?

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:07.410
Right.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:08.190
The first time.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.420
I'll be right there.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:10.800
Mitchell, That was it. That was the

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:11.850
call. I'm going in.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.740
Due to budget cuts, my position as

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.300
middle school music teacher has been

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.610
eliminated. So I've been working as a

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:18.780
high school sub.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.700
Cha-ching. I never know when I'll be

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.310
summoned to swoop into action.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.900
I'm kind of like Batman, but except for

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.510
a bat signal, I get a phone call.

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.320
Yeah, you found the one difference.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.290
I did my best to cram for my lecture on

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:34.110
the Revolutionary War, but all those

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.450
names and dates, it's all so dry.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.250
Where's the drama?

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.800
Good morrow. Oh, boy.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.300
Well, what is all this strange garb you

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.090
adorn? Are you trappers from the

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:52.530
Canadian provinces?

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.720
Are you here to sell your beavers?

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.280
Who are you?

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.410
The £0.64 question.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.710
I crossed the Delaware during the

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:03.300
Revolutionary War.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:07.110
I spent a brutal winter in Valley

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:08.970
Forge. Who am I?

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:11.120
I have no idea.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:12.830
I swear. I don't know who this man is.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:15.140
I'm George Washington.

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:16.190
Of course.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:17.540
Our syllabus says we're supposed to

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:18.890
cover Native Americans on the eve of

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:19.670
colonization.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:21.710
Yes, Native Americans.

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:25.130
Indians. A majestic, peaceful people

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:27.260
who lived off the land and cried when

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:28.250
they saw litter.

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:30.440
The textbook says many tribes were often

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.030
at war with allegiances shifting all of

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:32.450
the shifting.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:33.200
All the time.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.740
So were the Indians friends with the

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:37.910
colonists or not?

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:40.490
Oh, yes, I know one Indian who was

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:41.870
friends with a construction worker,

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:43.670
biker and traffic cop.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:46.340
Nothing. Seriously?

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.050
Nothing. Okay. Your parents are going

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:49.280
to love that joke.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:51.380
The Native Americans and the settlers

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:53.780
had two completely different ideas of

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:54.980
land ownership.

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:57.080
Eventually, these differences would

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:58.160
lead to war.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:01:59.600
Oh.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:01.400
Look. Goosebumps.

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:04.490
Okay. Yes.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:06.260
Class dismissed.

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:10.050
We did it. Thank you so much for

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:11.070
stepping in.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:12.900
Oh, and I promise tomorrow I will do my

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.760
best to be more prepared tomorrow.

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:16.020
Why won't Mrs. Hurley be back?

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:18.060
Well, I don't want to be indelicate, but

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:19.440
the good news is, is I might be your

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:20.550
permanent teacher.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.320
I don't want you to be my permanent

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:22.740
teacher.

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:23.790
Oh, what, you'd rather have a raging

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:24.480
alcoholic?

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.580
Listen to me. I have worked nonstop to

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:27.870
build the perfect academic record, and

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:29.160
I'm not going to let you screw it up

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.830
now. I have an AP test in 160 days, and

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.420
I need to ace it.

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:35.400
Can you get me there or not?

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:38.270
I can rally like the brave men of the

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:38.900
Alamo.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:40.670
You do realize that all the men of the

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:41.150
Alamo died.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:41.810
They all died.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.320
Set! Hike!

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:45.890
Oh, hey. You're going the wrong way.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:46.970
That's the wrong way.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.440
No, wait. I'm sorry.

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:49.100
You're right.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:51.770
Excuse me, Principal Brown.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.290
Yikes. And, you know, most subs just

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:55.460
play a movie. All right?

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:57.020
Do something different, guys.

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:59.600
Listen, I can't be your history teacher.

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:02.000
Those kids work so hard, and they

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.130
deserve someone who knows the material

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:05.930
and can inspire them.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:08.090
So if you say so.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.040
Hey, I was wondering, what kind of play

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:10.790
was that you were running? Was that

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:11.900
supposed to be a slant?

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:13.550
A freshman coach quit. I'm just a

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:14.780
glorified babysitter.

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:16.520
Well, your receiver needs to learn to

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:17.720
run his routes, or the quarterback's

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.070
never going to be able to hit him. I

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:20.030
played in college.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:21.680
Oh, okay. Hey, Tyler, you need to learn

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:22.790
to run your routes.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:23.840
What routes?

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:26.060
Yeah, What routes?

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:29.030
Well, you got to line up here.

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:30.560
Take three steps.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:31.730
One, two, three.

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:33.950
Plant right open, left, 45 degrees up

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:35.420
the field. Okay, why don't we try it

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:36.510
again? Try it again.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.270
Ten. Put some zip on the ball.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.000
18.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:40.410
Hut, Hut! Hike!

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:43.400
Hit him. Better.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.480
Better. Good job.

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:46.340
Circle back up.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.110
All right. Anyway, thank you for the

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:48.980
opportunity. Hey. Hey.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:50.090
How would you like to take over this

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:50.570
team?

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.150
Oh, well, that's an interesting offer.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:54.470
How much does it pay? Nothing.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.310
Are you firm on that?

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:56.960
Yeah, but there's a gym teacher position

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:58.130
available. It's all yours if you.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:03:59.360
Coach, can I wear shorts?

00:03:59.390 --> 00:03:59.660
Yeah.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:00.620
And you get a whistle, too?

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:01.790
Oh, I always get a whistle when I wear

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:04.550
shorts. I humbly accept your offer.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:06.050
Huddle up, boys.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:07.340
Let's go. Hustle.

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:08.570
Do you know what hustle means?

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:09.230
Ten.

